tion "To evaluate, we substitute $t=3$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(3) & =\\left\\langle {\\log }_{5}⁡({3}^{2}+16),\\,\\tan \\,\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{9}\\right),\\,{3}^{3}-6(3)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle {\\log }_{5}⁡(25),\\,\\tan \\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right),\\,27-18\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "526cac9d-bee9-5e96-9ea8-424944084161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427581} {:answer/id #uuid "6abd17a0-d501-55cc-8f71-616667496008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨6,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427582} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea49735-c879-5e56-98a2-6234975c2ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨12,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427583} {:answer/id #uuid "b978f470-a67c-5051-bacf-d5ebee33e3d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨7,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427586} {:answer/id #uuid "f5dd3736-c763-5b87-9410-dfb184b766a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨7,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427587}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427587} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff91b146-326d-518f-b02c-b93f9c2da44f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e765d7bb-3916-55f5-973d-5d131400a89f" :question/math-academy-id "q-123191" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\left\\langle 2t-5,\\,\\frac{4t+24}{t}\\right\\rangle ,$ calculate $r(6).$" :question/worked-solution "We  substitute $t=6$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(6) & =\\left\\langle 2\\cdot 6-5,\\,\\frac{4\\cdot 6+24}{6}\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨7,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4c60dd5-4f2f-5247-b508-e4412be02a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "31.68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540888}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540888} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f220aba-10fa-5140-91ce-bb3c746dbdc3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f4a5e43e-e7a6-55b0-a709-f89ec3a86933" :question/math-academy-id "q-133293" :question/problem "Let $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$ be the position vector of the eagle. Find the distance between the eagle and its nest at time $t=5\\,\\text{s},$ rounded to two decimal places.\n\nThe eagle is approximately$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$ away from its nest after $t=5$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "Since the nest is at the origin, the distance between the bird and its nest at time $t=5$ is $|r(5)|.$\n\nWe know that $y(5)=\\frac{95}{3}.$ Evaluating the function at $t=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(5) & =\\left\\langle \\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{5}{5}\\right),\\frac{95}{3}\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{95}{3}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(5)| & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{95}{3}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}+\\frac{9\\,025}{9}} \\\\  & ≈31.68\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575600 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c481408a-4444-530b-b268-67fbe75e182d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575296}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575296} :answer-field/id #uuid "2627111a-37e8-5d2c-8a5b-4d5136c68472" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8324fe7b-ac3f-57ba-80f6-ed595d15ca83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575183}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575183} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c8d376b-9f7b-5064-964a-ded341c098b6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575437} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "354b471b-f02d-5a8f-b605-c9b1d7cfa995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575039}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575039} :answer-field/id #uuid "54256760-b370-56e1-8f9d-274cd9ac9901" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cc70b07d-530b-5e77-9200-c7de006703f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-348662" :question/problem "What is the value of $$\n\\displaystyle g(t)=\\left\\langle {3}^{\\,t-1},\\,{\\log }_{3}⁡({t}^{2}+2t),\\,{sec}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}\\right)-1\\right\\rangle \n$$ at $t=1?$\n\n$g(1)=⟨$\n{{field-1}} $,\\,$\n{{field-2}} $,\\,$\n{{field-3}} $⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate, we substitute $t=1$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(1) & =\\left\\langle {3}^{1-1},\\,{\\log }_{3}⁡({1}^{2}+2(1)),\\,{sec}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-1\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,{\\log }_{3}⁡(3),\\,{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575615 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30dfc837-d5c1-5761-8aca-09d8e183f2c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575033}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575033} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8dd47c6-0daf-57eb-b7fa-e36f8f40c1d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e8bf0613-dc2d-57fb-b4e9-45d51faad202" :question/math-academy-id "q-348682" :question/problem "Given that $$\n\\displaystyle r(t)=\\left\\langle \\cos \\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{4}{t-1}\\right\\rangle ,\n$$ what is $|r(3)|?$\n\n$|r(3)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =\\left\\langle \\cos \\,\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{4}{3-1}\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(3)| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575620 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e550028-3605-535d-afc4-0b67b596e1d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574997} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd5b5cd-005e-5343-bec2-584e99c95568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575117} {:answer/id #uuid "6969e4a1-4a1e-5a38-83f0-7effe12a76ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575136} {:answer/id #uuid "cef7cdb8-1750-586d-9b65-5c0a924fd3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575315} {:answer/id #uuid "f6712659-f7f2-5848-8213-91e6b729c7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575385}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574997} :answer-field/id #uuid "760957fd-b385-5f58-b025-bc8ecf6a9ef0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f479be92-cf45-5de7-9956-484ec8fcce81" :question/math-academy-id "q-161508" :question/problem "What is the value of $$\n\\displaystyle f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(2t+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate, we substitute $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the value of $f(t)$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186603003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c658892-cfff-5719-9466-85e185302033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602581} {:answer/id #uuid "162529db-94e2-53e6-942e-41bc0fe6f25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602593} {:answer/id #uuid "868ed72d-7c51-5c3b-b2d7-3ce9dce4d3f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602713} {:answer/id #uuid "87f93eea-f487-5a46-bd13-0e7e3ca86d2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602715} {:answer/id #uuid "d8988b60-84f4-5037-ab2c-83e7fbb5b849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602829}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602581} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ec44893-e55c-5466-aaa6-28a7e6e5a591" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "13e1a728-9acf-5c9e-b21e-002241f3ccbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-123215" :question/problem "Find $|r(4)|$ given that $r(t)=\\left\\langle \\frac{16}{{t}^{2}},\\,t-3,\\,6-2t\\right\\rangle .$" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(4) & =\\left\\langle \\frac{16}{{4}^{2}},\\,4-3,\\,6-2(4)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(4)| & =\\sqrt{{(1)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186603017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5cfe6ba-5ca8-5734-8cd6-44b79387eae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602847}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602847} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d1a0d86-6788-5438-8441-a7af22a7294c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d09aadcc-c05a-57eb-85d9-edf991428e3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602814}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602814} :answer-field/id #uuid "96476559-baca-5167-a6fb-c5d79df41ea0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2737bc55-42bf-5b9f-a99a-930a65660299" :question/math-academy-id "q-348643" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\left\\langle t+4,\\,\\frac{3t+1}{t}\\right\\rangle ,$ calculate $r(3).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$r(3)=⟨$\n{{field-1}} $,$\n\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $t=3$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =\\left\\langle 3+4,\\,\\frac{3(3)+1}{3}\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle 7,\\,\\frac{10}{3}\\right\\rangle .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186603026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a183daf-5346-561d-976f-c75854a18657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602597}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602597} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd429eb-f38d-582b-8ead-2f44c7fae8d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "35b01f91-97de-5c92-90e3-e5c3ee5fc4cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-346881" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=\\left\\langle \\sqrt{\\frac{12}{t+1}},\\,{t}^{2}-8\\right\\rangle ,$ what is $|r(3)|?$\n\n$|r(3)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =\\left\\langle \\sqrt{\\frac{12}{3+1}},\\,{3}^{2}-8\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\sqrt{\\frac{12}{4}},\\,1\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(3)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3+1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]
